{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} |''^```'\"' PLAN.md\"","aggregated_output":"1:# PLAN: an original open-world mercenary game inspired by Far Cry 2\n13:## 1. The game\n46:## 2. Foundation\n48:### 2.1 Get the pieces\n50:```sh\n51:# in the dev folder\n60:```\n74:### 2.2 Build into one file (VERIFIED)\n82:### 2.3 The kit, section by section\n109:### 2.4 Engine facts that will otherwise cost you hours\n124:## 3. The world\n130:### Sites (metres east, metres south)\n165:### Terrain (rewrite `baseH` and `color`)\n189:### Time, wind, weather\n197:## 4. The player and the hands\n199:### Controls (prompts always come from `game.input.label(action)`)\n221:### Moving\n225:### Holding things (pillar 3)\n237:### Health\n245:### The rasp (salt lung)\n257:## 5. Weapons and wear\n289:## 6. Fire\n318:## 7. Vehicles\n350:## 8. People\n352:### Factions\n363:### Soldier AI (extend `raiderStep`; keep its sight, hearing, bursts, strafing, hunt)\n372:### Guard posts and papers\n379:### Buddies\n413:## 9. Story and writing\n415:### Tone (TASK.md: a writing style like the source's)\n427:### Cast\n438:### The radio (vehicle radio, random order; write 20 more)\n446:### Barks (gibberish with subtitle; write 8 per faction)\n453:### Contracts (table `CONTRACTS`; an order the player mostly can't break)\n489:### The Soundings (eight survey stakes across the basin, each a tin box on a tripod)\n502:### The Sill and the endings\n518:## 10. Money, safe houses, saves\n527:## 11. Screens and 10-foot UX\n574:## 12. Sound (all generated; no audio files)\n596:## 13. Multiplayer: \"Salvage Rights\"\n602:```html\n609:```\n651:## 14. Testing\n682:## 15. Build order\n703:### Finish\n713:## 16. TASK.md coverage\n743:## Appendix A: verified recipes\n747:### A1. Build script and page\n749:```js\n777:```\n780:### A2. A thing held in the hand: map, logbook, shop card, locator face\n784:```js\n792:```\n795:### A3. Time of day\n799:```js\n828:```\n830:### A4. Fire: mask, spread, flames, smoke\n832:```js\n881:```\n884:### A5. Water (the Remnant, the reservoir, the flood)\n886:```js\n894:```\n896:### A6. Boot order for the hub (the only order that passed at 4 players)\n898:```js\n912:```\n915:### A7. Settings, TV size, touch notice\n917:```js\n923:```\n925:```css\n929:```\n931:### A8. Test helpers (Python)\n933:```python\n934:# a controller, for add_init_script: then set window.__pad.buttons[7] = {pressed:True,...} and bump timestamp\n939:# the hub's harness: serve hub/ on a port the OS picks, stop only that PID\n944:# page.goto(f'http://127.0.0.1:{port}/harness.html?game=game.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=standard&play=8000')\n945:# page.wait_for_selector('body[data-complete=\"true\"]', timeout=300000); report = page.evaluate('() => window.__hubCheck')   # report['pass'], report['checks']\n946:# finally: srv.terminate()\n947:```\n950:### A9. WebGPU in headless Chromium here\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
