{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,264p' engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"","aggregated_output":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge 3D v0.88.0: real 3D worlds under my-3D2dge games (three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3)\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n\nA 3D world, its physics and its camera under a my-3D2dge game. The 2D engine (engine/my-3d2dge.js) still runs the game:\nits exact fixed steps, scenes, input, pause menu, settings, touch buttons, sound, the rigs and their moves, the HUD. This\nmodule simulates and draws the world under the game's clear canvas. Everything is drawn by code: levels written as text,\ntextures pixel by pixel, characters by the 2D engine's rigs (as cards, or as 3D puppets on the same joints), props and\npickups from four shapes. No image, model or sound files.\n\nAGENTS: this header is the whole manual for the 3D side; the API card (API.md) covers the 2D side (E.Game, input, rigs,\nmoves, E.font, E.ui, E.Menu, audio). Read the code below to debug it, or to change it (it is yours to change, in any\nway you see fit): its sections start with \"/* ===\" and a number.\n\n## Host it (served: browsers load modules only over http; npx serve at the repository's root, or my-3d2dge.vercel.app)\n<script type=\"importmap\">{ \"imports\": { \"three\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\",\n  \"three/webgpu\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js\", \"three/tsl\": \"/vendor/three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js\",\n  \"@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat\": \"/vendor/rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js\" } }</script>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; overflow: hidden; background: #000 }</style>\n<div id=\"stage\" style=\"position:relative;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:hidden\">\n  <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas><canvas id=\"screen\" style=\"position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%\"></canvas></div>\n<script src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge.js\"></script>                   the 2D engine, a classic script, first\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"/dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js\"></script>  this file\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"game.js\"></script>                your game, a module (const E = My3D2dge;)\nInlined into a page's own script tag instead, this file ends the page at its first closing script tag (this header has\nfour): write each with a backslash before its slash, as the build's single files do.\n\n## Mental model\n- The 2D engine's units: x east, y south, z up; 16 units = 1 metre = 1 tile; speeds in units a second; angles in\n  radians from +x toward +y (0 east, PI/2 south, -PI/2 north). The axes are left-handed (three.js's are right-handed):\n  a mesh of your own built in engine units comes out mirrored, its winding and turns flipped; place it in three.js's\n  (E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z): x, z, y over 16).\n- new E.Game({ ..., bg: null }): its canvas is clear, and the HUD draws on it over the 3D picture (r.overlay, r.text,\n  E.ui, E.font) in game pixels, r.W x r.H. res: 'ps1', expand: true as in the 2D games.\n- await E.World3D.init(game) once (a boot step), then new E.World3D(game, { level, ... }) for each level. In a scene:\n  update(dt) { your rules, then world.step(dt) } and draw(r) { world.draw(r), then your HUD }. Paused or frozen\n  (game.freeze), update doesn't run, so the world holds still and still draws. A frame between steps draws the actors\n  and the camera part way from the step before (game.alpha: even motion at 144 Hz); a pose set in onDraw is placed as set.\n- Deterministic: the world steps in the game's fixed steps; gameplay randomness comes from E.rng(seed); the camera's\n  pose is worked out in the steps. world.reset() then the same inputs give the same world.hash() on WebGPU, WebGL 2 and\n  run again. Gameplay never reads the picture or the GPU: it reads actors, props and the level.\n- The camera decides what \"up the stick\" means: move with world.camera.ground(game.input.move()).\n\n## Quick start: a complete game (collect the gems, mind the slimes)\n```js quickstart\nconst E = My3D2dge;\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: E.World3D.INPUT, menu: { settings: E.World3D.SETTINGS } });\nconst LEVEL = { rows: [\n  '################',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '#..g.....==..g.#',\n  '#........==....#',\n  '#..s.....^^....#',\n  '#.............s#',\n  '#..g...@....g..#',\n  '#t............t#',\n  '################'],\n  legend: { '=': { floor: 16 }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 16 }, g: { mark: 'gem' }, s: { mark: 'slime' }, '@': { mark: 'start' } } };\nlet world, hero, slimes, gems, hp, done;\nconst move = [0, 0];\nconst play = {\n  view: 'iso', views: ['iso', 'threequarter', 'topdown'], pausable: true, touch: ['jump'], camera: { zoom: [.6, 2] },\n  enter() {\n    world.reset(); const rnd = E.rng(1), s = world.marks.start[0];\n    hero = world.hero({ x: s.x, y: s.y, rig: new E.Humanoid({ colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86' } }) });\n    slimes = world.marks.slime.map(m => world.mob({ x: m.x, y: m.y, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6 }) }));\n    gems = world.marks.gem.map(m => world.thing('gem', m.x, m.y, m.z + 2, { spin: .5, bob: 3 }));\n    world.camera.follow(hero); hp = 3; done = false;\n    for (const e of slimes) e.data.t = rnd() * 2;\n  },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (game.input.pressed('camera')) world.camera.set(world.camera.mode === 'view' ? 'chase' : 'view');\n    world.camera.ground(game.input.move(), move);\n    hero.vx = E.approach(hero.vx, move[0] * 90, 900 * dt); hero.vy = E.approach(hero.vy, move[1] * 90, 900 * dt);\n    if (Math.hypot(move[0], move[1]) > .1) hero.facing = Math.atan2(move[1], move[0]);\n    if (hero.grounded && game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(170);\n    for (const e of slimes) {   // hop at the hero now and then; touch one: a heart lost, knocked back\n      if ((e.data.t -= dt) < 0 && e.grounded) { e.data.t = 1.2; const a = Math.atan2(hero.y - e.y, hero.x - e.x); e.vx = Math.cos(a) * 60; e.vy = Math.sin(a) * 60; e.vz = 140; e.facing = a; }\n      if (Math.hypot(e.x - hero.x, e.y - hero.y) < 11 && Math.abs(e.z - hero.z) < 10 && !(hero.data.inv > 0)) { hp--; hero.data.inv = 1; hero.push((hero.x - e.x) * 12, (hero.y - e.y) * 12, 120); game.shake(3); }\n    }\n    hero.data.inv = (hero.data.inv || 0) - dt;\n    for (const t of world.touching(hero, 'gem')) { world.remove(t); gems.splice(gems.indexOf(t), 1); game.particles.glints(t.x, t.y, t.z + 6, 8, '#bff8ff'); }\n    if (!done && (!gems.length || hp <= 0)) { done = true; game.note(gems.length ? 'OUCH!' : 'ALL GEMS!', 2); game.after(2, () => game.go('play')); }\n    world.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    world.draw(r);\n    r.overlay(g => { E.ui.hearts(g, 6, 6, Math.max(0, hp), 3); E.font.text(g, 'GEMS ' + gems.length, 6, 18, '#bff8ff'); });\n  }\n};\ngame.start({ scenes: { play }, scene: 'play', boot: { steps: [\n  ['The 3D engine', () => E.World3D.init(game)],\n  ['The level', () => { world = new E.World3D(game, { level: LEVEL }); world.prepare(); }]] } });\n```\n\n## The level: text, one character per tile; row 0 is north\nlevel: { rows, legend, ground, side, colors, bottom }. A legend entry says what its character is (the defaults: '#' wall\n48, 'w' wall 12, 'P' pillar 56, '.' floor, ' ' pit, 't' brazier):\n  { floor: h }        walkable at height h (0 the ground; above 0 a raised floor, solid to the ground)\n  { wall: h }         a solid block h tall, cut low where it stands between a view camera and the level (cut: false)\n  { pillar: h }       each block of these tiles is one pillar, cut to a stump when it hides the target\n  { stairs: 'n'|'s'|'e'|'w', from: 0, floor: 16 }   rising toward that side, from height `from` to `floor`\n  { platform: h, thick: 4 }   a slab in the air, its top at h (walk under it); add pit: true for nothing below\n  { pit: true }       no floor: a body that falls in is lost (actor.fell)\n  { torch: true }     a brazier with a flickering light (the lights go to the torches nearest the target)\n  { mark: 'name' }    a spot: world.marks.name -> [{ x, y, z, cx, cy }] (the tile's centre, on its surface)\n  { shape: 'bench', facing, scale, mats, solid }   a shape standing on the tile (world.shape), walked round when solid\nand its look: ground ('flagstone' 'grass' 'dirt' 'sand' 'snow' 'planks' 'tiles' 'plain' 'water' 'lava', or (x, y) =>\n[r, g, b]) with colors { base, dark, light }, side ('brick' 'block' 'earth' 'planks' 'metal') with color (and top, line).\nThe level's ground is every tile's default; its side styles the floors' edges, its wallSide the walls ('brick'; a tile's\nown side wins). Add looks: E.World3D.GROUND.name, E.World3D.SIDE.name.\n\n## The world: new E.World3D(game, o)\no: { level, look: 'card' | 'puppet', res: 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full', gravity: 480, sky: '#06050b' or [top,\nhorizon], fog: { color, near, far } (units past the target) or false, ambient: [sky, ground, intensity], sun: { color,\nintensity, dir: [x, y, z] (it shines along it), area, shadow }, torchLights: 6, torchShadows: 1, torchPower: 30,\nlights: 2 (your own), spots: 0 (flashlights), glowLights: 4, shadows, outlines, filter, camera: { mode, proj, fov, chase, ... }, terrain (an open\nworld instead of the level: below), overlay: { fov } (first person: below), onDraw: (world, r) => {} (your own 3D drawing\neach frame, whichever scene draws the world) }\n  world.step(dt) / world.draw(r) / world.reset() / world.hash([your numbers]) / world.prepare() (build the shaders now)\n  world.dispose(): frees a world (its physics, meshes and textures); dispose a level's world before making the next\n  world.width, depth (units), mw, mh (tiles), bottom, marks, torches, actors, props, platforms, things, time, stats\n  world.ground(x, y)   the ground's height (a wall's top on a wall; bottom over a pit)\n  world.floorAt(x, y, z)   the surface a body at height z stands on or falls to (platforms too)\n  world.topH(x, y)     the top of whatever stands there (shots stop below it)\n  world.tile(cx, cy), spec(cx, cy), solidTile(cx, cy)   the level's character, its legend entry, walls and pillars\n  world.flow() -> flow: flow.to(x, y) aims it; flow.dir(x, y, out) -> the way there ([x, y], or null: go straight);\n      it climbs stairs and gentle slopes and drops off ledges, never jumps\n  world.randomFloor(rnd, minDist, fx, fy) -> [x, y]; world.clear(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1) -> a clear line of sight?\n  world.ray(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len, { skip: actor(s), level: true (sight lines), down }) -> the first hit { x, y, z, nx,\n      ny, nz, dist, actor, prop, ground } or null: hitscan, ledges, feet on the ground\n  world.block({ x, y, z, w, d, h, yaw } | { x, y, z, r, h }): an invisible fixed collider (walls you draw your own way;\n      z its base, as for world.box, world.thing and world.shape)\n  world.near(x, y, r, kind) -> actors within r; world.touching(actor, kind) -> things it touches\n  world.project(x, y, z) -> [x, y] in game pixels for the HUD (null behind the camera)\n  world.remove(actor | prop | platform | thing)\n\n## Actors: world.hero(o) and world.mob(o)\nhero: a kinematic capsule walked by Rapier's character controller: it slides along walls, climbs stairs and slopes,\nsteps up curbs, rides moving platforms, pushes crates and shoves mobs. mob: a dynamic body; the crowd pushes and piles\nup by itself, knockback is momentum. o: { x, y, z, rig: new E.Humanoid(...) | blob: new E.Blob(...) | orb: { color, r },\nr, half (the capsule: radius, half its straight part; half 0 a ball), facing, fly (no gravity), mass, trail (a color for\nthe rig's weapon trail), look ('card' | 'puppet' for this one), shadow, pose: false (you pose it yourself) }\nEach step you set what it wants: a.vx, a.vy (units a second on the ground: E.approach toward a target speed), a.jump(v)\nor a.vz, a.facing, a.anim (what its rig does: { attack: move.state, pose: 'cheer' | 'die' | 'cast', hurt, dash, expr };\na blob's { squash, look: [dx, dy], squint, flap }); world.step moves it, reads back a.x, a.y, a.z (its feet), a.vx,\na.vy, a.vz, a.grounded, a.landed (this step), a.fell (dropped below the level), and poses its rig.\n  a.place(x, y, z), a.push(vx, vy, vz) (knockback), a.setSolid(false) (fallen: it stops blocking the others), a.remove(),\n  a.resize(half) (a crouch, a slide: the capsule shorter, the feet kept; look up with world.ray before standing)\n  a.flash (a hit flash while above 0: count it down yourself, a.flash -= dt), a.fade (0..1), a.sink (units drawn into the floor: spawning, sinking away), a.visible,\n  a.data (yours). E.Attack, E.Combo and E.MOVES work as in 2D: attack.hits(list, e => E.inArc(a, a.facing, e, range,\n  half), e => ...) on actors.\n\n## Props, platforms and things\n  world.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing, scale, mats, flip, params, solid: true }): a shape (docs/ASSETS.md: an E.SHAPES id,\n  a store set's 'SET:id' after E.addAssets, or an entry) in 3D, from the 2D engine's parts and materials, solid as\n  map.solid's box. A reset takes yours away (the legend's stand again); world.shapes holds them; world.remove(s)\n  world.crate(x, y, z, yaw), world.barrel(x, y, z): dynamic bodies (z their centre; left out, on the floor); world.knock(p, fromX, fromY, dv, up) throws one;\n  world.box({ x, y, z, w, d, h, color, side, fixed, mass }); a prop has x, y, z, q (its rotation), data\n  world.platform({ w, d, h, path: [[x, y, z], ...] (its top's points), speed, wait, loop, side, color }): a platform that\n  moves (there and back, or round with loop); heroes on it ride it, bodies on it are carried\n  world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o): drawn by code: coin gem heart key star potion chest door flag sign lever pad spring\n  tree bush rock mushroom fence crystal trunk (an item box) typewriter (a save point); o: { yaw, spin (turns a second),\n  bob, size, color, open (0..1), on, solid: true | [w, d, h] (a block where it stands: world.setSolid(t, false) opens\n  it), data }. Add a kind:\n  E.World3D.THINGS.lamp = (pen, t, time) => { pen.tube(0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 20, 1, '#555').glow(0, 0, 21, 2, '#ffd36a'); }\n  A door: { w (32, across its local x), h (40), swing: true (leaves on hinges; else a gate that rises), locked: 'iron' (a\n  key's id) }. world.reach(hero, 14, kinds) -> the thing in front of it within reach (what a check button acts on);\n  world.unlock(door, inv) -> 'open' | 'unlocked' (the key taken from an E.RPG inventory) | 'locked';\n  world.through(door, hero, { then }): the door opening between rooms (Resident Evil's): the camera goes through as it\n  swings open, the hero comes out beyond it; while world.passing the world holds still: skip your rules\n\n## Drawing for one frame (in draw, before world.draw(r))\n  world.arc(x, y, z, r0, r1, a0, a1, color, alpha): a flat arc on the ground (a telegraph)\n  world.glow(x, y, z, r, color, { core, light: true }): a glowing ball (a bolt); the first four asked for light the scene\n  world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll).box(x, y, z, w, d, h, color).ball(x, y, z, rx, ry, rz, color).tube(x0, y0, z0, x1,\n      y1, z1, r, color).cone(...base to tip).bar(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, w, t, color).glow(x, y, z, r, color)\n      .slab(x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1, ax, ay, az, w, t, color) (a box from one point to the other, w wide along a: any lean)\n  world.light({ color, reach, power, flicker }) (made once, with the world): a light; set its x, y, z and on each frame\n  world.flashlight(hero, { color, reach, angle, power, flicker: 0..1 (a failing bulb) }) (a world made with { spots: 1 }):\n  a spot from its hand along its facing, every frame, casting shadows; .on\n  game.particles (sparks, dust, bits, rings, glints, fire, text): drawn in 3D; they land on the level; text goes on the HUD\n  game.shake(n), game.flash(color), game.freeze(s), game.note(text): as in 2D\n\n## The camera: world.camera\n  modes: 'view' (the 2D engine's views as real 3D cameras following camera.target: game.view (game.nextView()),\n  game.yaw (game.rotateView(45)): the starter's shell binds V and [ ] to them, the engine no key; game.zoom (the wheel,\n  a pinch, Settings, where the scene's camera.zoom allows); proj 'persp' | 'ortho'; dist; walls in\n  front cut low), 'chase' (behind the target; it swings round behind as the target moves; a click captures the mouse to\n  turn it), 'first' (the target's eyes), 'fly', 'fixed' (camera.fixed = { x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }: your own),\n  'zones' (Resident Evil's: camera.zones = [{ box: [x0, y0, x1, y1], at: [x, y, z], look: [x, y, z] (fixed) | follow:\n  true (turning after the target) | rail: [[x, y, z], [x, y, z]] (sliding level with it), fov (framed for 4:3: a taller\n  screen widens it) }]: the target's zone is the camera, cut once it is camera.margin (8) units in (camera.zone,\n  camera.cuts); across a cut ground() keeps the old way while the stick is held)\n  camera: { capture: true (a click captures the mouse in any mode; camera.takeMouse(out) -> its [dx, dy] since the last\n  call: turn your own camera), near, far (units) }; camera.target also sizes the outlines and centres the sun's shadow\n  camera.set(mode), camera.follow(actor), camera.ground(move, out) -> the stick turned to the ground,\n  camera.aim(actor) -> the angle the mouse (on the floor) or right stick points from it, or null; camera.heading,\n  camera.pose, camera.chase = { pitch, dist, fov, height, auto }, camera.first = { pitch, fov }\n  camera.steer(hero, move, dt, out) -> the way to go by the player's setting (game.settings.define(E.World3D.CONTROLS)):\n  ground(), or tank controls (up forward along hero.facing, down back, left and right turn it: set facing yourself only\n  when !camera.tank)\n  Lock-on (Zelda's targeting): camera.lock(hero, mobs, { range: 160 }) -> the one in sight (alive, in range, a clear\n  line) nearest where hero faces, or null; camera.cycle(mobs, 1 | -1) the next round the hero; camera.unlock();\n  camera.lockOn. The chase and first cameras swing behind the hero to frame both, the view frames both, ground() strafes\n  round it, a reticle marks it (camera.reticle: a color, false); it lets go when the target dies (alive = false), leaves\n  or goes past 1.25 times the range. Turn the hero to it yourself\n\n## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\nterrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\ncells), far (draw distance), physics (heightfields this near an actor), detail (1.7), rock: { colors, band, slope: [s0,\ns1] } (strata where it steepens), speckle, mottle, bottom }. Streamed: a chunk is sampled when first asked about, its\ncollider made near actors (world.step), its meshes near the camera (world.draw: finer near). world.ground, floorAt, topH\nand world.terrain.normal(x, y) read the triangles Rapier collides with; flow() goes straight. sky: { top, horizon, ground,\nsun, haze } is a dome; fog: { color, near, far }. Keep height() fast: it runs per sample.\n\n## Vehicles, tracks, flight (the RACING and FLIGHT slices show them)\nworld.vehicle({ kind: 'kart' | 'car' | 'hover', x, y, z, angle, rig (its driver, seated), color, and the drive module's\nE.Car options over the kind's (top, accel, brake, turn, grip, drift, hop...), surfaces, ground: (x, y) => tag }): a ball\nRapier rolls (walls, bumps, ramps, jumps) steered by E.Car's arcade handling; an actor. Each step v.update(dt, null,\n{ steer, gas, brake, drift }) (or an input), then world.step; it reads speed, slide, angle, drifting, charge (a kart's\ndrift boost), boostT, onGround, surface ('road', 'boost', a track's off, the level's ground: grass, sand... slow it),\nbumped; v.boost(sec, power), v.spinOut(sec). E.Race (the drive module) races vehicles as it races E.Cars.\nworld.track({ path: new E.Path(points [x, y, z], { closed: true, smooth: 'catmull' }), width: 96, bank: .25 (radians at\nthe tightest bends), walls: true, kerb: 8, pads: [[d, across]] (boost pads), gaps: [[d0, d1, side]] (no wall: a\nshortcut's way off), off (the surface beside it, 'grass'; null: the ground's own), surface: 'road' (a shortcut's\n'dirt'), color, line }): the road and its walls, drawn\nand solid (heights in the path: hills, a hump to jump; banked about the low edge); track.at(d) -> { x, y, z, angle, bank\n}, track.where(x, y) -> { d, across, z }, track.surface(x, y). A terrain under it keeps below it (your height function).\nworld.flyer({ x, y, z, yaw, speed: 300, min, max (brake, boost), turn, climb, bank, invert, low (least height), bounds:\n[x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] | rail: { path, speed, w, h } (Star Fox: the rail's point rides on, the ship moves about a w x h\nwindow across it) }): each step f.update(dt, { steer: [x, y], boost, brake, roll: -1 | 1 (a barrel roll: f.rolling),\nloop }); f.x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, speed, frame (the rail's point), hitGround; f.seek(list, { cone, range }): what a\ncharged shot locks on; f.at(): where to draw it this frame. world.pen.at(x, y, z, yaw, size, pitch, roll) tips the pen.\ncamera 'behind': behind the target's heading (yaw, angle or facing) and pitch, swinging after it (camera.behind = { dist,\nheight, ahead, lag, fov, roll }): a kart's camera, a ship's (follow f.frame on a rail).\nSplit screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\nanswers in the viewport drawn last; no filter while split.\n\n## First person and third: a shooter (the starter's SHOOTER slice shows it all)\ncamera 'fixed' with capture: each step turn by camera.takeMouse(), set camera.fixed (the eyes, or over the shoulder pulled\nin by world.ray). overlay: { fov } makes world.overlay = { scene, camera, pen, on }: drawn after the world, its depth\ncleared (the gun never sinks into a wall), lit like the world. overlay.pen is a pen in the eye's frame (engine units: x\nahead, y right, z up): draw the arms and gun in onDraw; world.pen there draws bodies (the pens empty after each frame).\n\n## The look\n  world.look = 'card' | 'puppet'; world.res = 'pixels' | 'balanced' | 'full'; world.shadows; world.outlines\n  world.filter = { look: 'clean' | 'cel' (Comic cel: flat bands of light, ink) | 'pixel' (big dithered pixels), apply:\n  'all' | 'objects' | 'env', bloom, fxaa, bands, ink, inkW, punch, px, levels, dither }\n  E.World3D.SETTINGS in the game's menu lets the player pick the look, the picture, shadows and the filter.\n  E.World3D.INPUT: WASD or arrows move, Space jumps, J or a click attacks, Shift dashes, E skill, Q lock, C camera.\n\n## Your own three.js\nE.THREE (three/webgpu), E.TSL, E.RAPIER; world.scene, world.pw (Rapier's world), E.World3D.toThree(x, y, z) (engine\nunits to three's metres, y up). The rules: WebGPURenderer and node materials only (MeshLambertNodeMaterial,\nMeshToonNodeMaterial, MeshBasicNodeMaterial, TSL): never WebGLRenderer, ShaderMaterial, onBeforeCompile, EffectComposer or\nthree/addons (not vendored); no compute shaders or storage buffers; nothing read back from the GPU. An InstancedMesh with\nover 1,000 instances never uses DynamicDrawUsage (r182 drops its updates). Make meshes and lights when the world is made,\nnot mid-game (a new material builds its shader: a stall).\n\n## Tests\nHeadless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\nruns fixed steps at once; game.input.hold / tap script input. The kits expose window.__game.\n*/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat src/00-shell.js src/90-start.js && sed -n '1,146p' src/30-shooter.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat src/00-shell.js src/90-start.js && sed -n '1,146p' src/30-shooter.js\"","aggregated_output":"/* ============================== GAME START ==============================\n * MY-3D2DGE 3D STARTER: a title menu and the 3D slices (a 3D genre kit file holds one). Each slice is a complete small\n * 3D game, written to be copied and changed: its own header (below this shell) says what it plays, its keys and touch\n * controls, its deep links and how it works. The 3D engine's manual (the header of engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js) says how a\n * game runs on a 3D world: E.Game as in 2D with bg: null, world.step(dt) in update, world.draw(r) then the HUD in draw.\n * THE SHELL'S KEYS: M mutes; in a slice whose camera follows the game's view, V changes the view, [ ] turn it and 0\n * resets it (the wheel, - and = zoom where the scene allows); the pause menu's Display has the 3D settings\n * (characters as cards or puppets, the picture's resolution, shadows).\n * To make your own game: change the slice closest to your genre into yours, with its own title, play and game-over\n * scenes, and delete the slices you do not use; this shell (the game, its scenes, the boot steps) stays unless you replace\n * it. Deep links: #<slice> starts a slice, #<slice>/<part> jumps into a part.\n * ======================================================================== */\nconst E = My3D2dge, W3 = E.World3D, { clamp, lerp, approach, TAU } = E;\n\n/* ---- SHELL: one game, several scenes, each slice with its own world ----\n * bg: null keeps the game's canvas clear over the 3D picture; E.World3D.INPUT: WASD move, Space jump, J or a click\n * attack, Shift dash, E skill, C camera; E.World3D.SETTINGS: the 3D settings in the pause menu */\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, bg: null, input: W3.INPUT, menu: { settings: W3.SETTINGS } });\nconst P = game.particles, A = game.audio;\nconst scenes = {}, BOOT = [];    // BOOT: the slices' heavy setup, [label, fn] steps run behind the boot screen\n// each slice: its scene's id, its title entry, a line about it, and its family (the title groups them under it)\nconst SLICES = [\n  { id: 'action', label: 'ACTION', about: 'A 3D ARENA: COMBOS, DASHES AND WAVES', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'platformer', label: 'PLATFORMER', about: 'A 3D COURSE: ISLANDS, PLATFORMS AND COINS', family: 'PLATFORM' },\n  { id: 'shooter', label: 'SHOOTER', about: 'AN OPEN WORLD: MOVE, CLIMB AND FIGHT, FIRST OR THIRD PERSON', family: 'SHOOTER' },\n  { id: 'horror', label: 'HORROR', about: 'A MANSION BY FLASHLIGHT: FIXED CAMERAS, FEW BULLETS', family: 'ACTION ADVENTURE' },\n  { id: 'racing', label: 'RACING', about: 'A KART CIRCUIT: DRIFTS, ITEMS, A SHORTCUT, TWO PLAYERS', family: 'RACING' },\n  { id: 'flight', label: 'FLIGHT', about: 'ON RAILS TO THE BASE, A BOSS IN FREE FLIGHT', family: 'SHOOTER' },\n  { id: 'crawler', label: 'CRAWLER', about: 'A DUNGEON IN FIRST PERSON: A PARTY OF FOUR, A CELL AT A TIME', family: 'RPG' }\n];\n// a prompt in the player's own controls ('J Sword', 'X Sword', 'ATTACK Sword' on a touch screen)\n// (a phone or tablet before its first touch counts too: a coarse pointer and nothing else used yet)\nconst coarse = typeof matchMedia === 'function' && matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\nconst prompt = (a, word) => game.input.label(a) + ' ' + word, touch = () => game.input.lastDevice === 'touch' || (coarse && game.input.lastDevice === 'keyboard');\n// START picks too (the touch START, a pad's Start), as Enter does\nconst pickOnStart = m => { if (game.input.pressed('start')) { game.input.consumeAll(); m.onPick(m.i, m.items[m.i]); } };\nlet active = null;               // the world of the scene that is playing (the shared keys turn its camera)\n\n/* ---- the camera: C cycles the view, the chase camera and first person; V, [ ] and 0 work on the view (and turn the\n * others) ---- */\nconst CAMS = ['view', 'chase', 'first'], CAM_NAME = { chase: 'CHASE CAMERA', first: 'FIRST PERSON' };\nconst viewName = () => game.view.label.toUpperCase() + ' VIEW';\n/** the camera key (input action 'camera'), read in a slice's update */\nfunction cameraKey(world) {\n  if (!game.input.pressed('camera')) return;\n  const c = world.camera, m = CAMS[(CAMS.indexOf(c.mode) + 1) % CAMS.length]; c.set(m); game.note(m === 'view' ? viewName() : CAM_NAME[m]);\n}\naddEventListener('keydown', e => {\n  if (e.repeat || e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey || e.altKey || game.paused) return;\n  if (e.code === 'KeyM') { A.mute(); return; }\n  if (active && ['fixed', 'zones'].includes(active.camera.mode)) return;   // (a slice that runs its own camera, or fixed cameras by room: its keys are its own)\n  if (e.code === 'KeyV') { game.nextView(); if (active) active.camera.set('view'); game.note(viewName()); }\n  else if (e.code === 'Digit0') { game.settings.set('zoom', 1); game.resetCamera(); game.note('CAMERA RESET'); }\n  else if (e.code === 'BracketLeft' || e.code === 'BracketRight') { game.rotateView(e.code === 'BracketLeft' ? -45 : 45); game.note('TURN ' + game.yaw); }\n});\n/** a dark veil over the 3D picture (the title's lower third, a game over) */\nconst veil = (g, r, y0, a = .55) => { g.save(); g.fillStyle = '#05030c'; g.globalAlpha = a; g.fillRect(0, y0, r.bw, r.bh - y0); g.restore(); g._c = null; };\n\n/* ---- TITLE: a little stage in 3D, the slices' heroes on it in torchlight, the camera turning round them ---- */\nconst TITLE_LEVEL = {\n  rows: [\n    '                    ',\n    ' ################## ',\n    ' #t......PP......t# ',\n    ' #.......PP.......# ',\n    ' #................# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #....========....# ',\n    ' #.....^^^^^^.....# ',\n    ' #t..............t# ',\n    ' #................# ',\n    '                    '],\n  legend: { '=': { floor: 8, side: 'block', color: '#4a4360' }, '^': { stairs: 'n', floor: 8 } }\n};\nlet title = null;\nconst TITLE_CAST = [\n  { x: -18, face: 0, rig: () => new E.Humanoid({ cape: { len: 6, width: 5, seg: 2.5 }, colors: { cloth: '#2f8f86', cape: '#c8452f', capeIn: '#7a2622', hair: '#2e2230' } }) },\n  { x: 18, face: 0, rig: () => new E.Humanoid({ weapon: null, hat: 'cap', build: 'heroic', colors: { cloth: '#d83a2a', pants: '#2f5fd0', glove: '#f0f0f0', hat: '#d83a2a' } }) }\n];\nBOOT.push(['The title stage', () => {\n  const w = new W3(game, { level: TITLE_LEVEL, fog: { near: 140, far: 600 }, torchShadows: 1 }), cx = w.width / 2, cy = 6.5 * 16;\n  const heroes = TITLE_CAST.map(c => { const a = w.hero({ x: cx + c.x, y: cy, rig: c.rig(), facing: Math.PI / 2 }); a.anim = { pose: null }; return a; });\n  const slime = w.mob({ x: cx - 44, y: cy + 30, blob: new E.Blob({ R: 6.2, face: 'front', ears: 'cat' }) }), wisp = w.mob({ x: cx + 44, y: cy + 24, orb: { color: '#c78bff' }, fly: true });\n  w.thing('star', cx, cy - 26, 8 + 12, { spin: .35, bob: 3 });\n  w.camera.set('fixed');\n  title = { world: w, cx, cy, heroes, slime, wisp, t: 0 };\n}]);\n/** the title's menu for the slices in this file: grouped by family when there are several (FamilyMenu, in 05-families.js:\n *  the reference editions carry it, a genre kit of one slice doesn't), else a plain E.Menu */\nconst menuOf = (slices, o) => new Set(slices.map(s => s.family)).size > 1 ? new FamilyMenu(slices, o) : new E.Menu(game, slices.map(s => s.label), o);\nlet titleMenu = null;   // (made at the start, once the file's slices are known)\nscenes.title = {\n  view: 'iso', input: W3.INPUT,\n  enter() { A.music('title'); active = null; game.resetCamera(); },\n  update(dt) {\n    if (!titleMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(titleMenu);\n    const T = title, w = T.world; T.t += dt;\n    // the camera turns slowly round the stage; the heroes swing now and then; the slime hops, the wisp hovers\n    const a = T.t * .18 + 2.2, d = 120;\n    w.camera.fixed = { x: T.cx + Math.cos(a) * d, y: T.cy + Math.sin(a) * d, z: 58, yaw: a + Math.PI, pitch: -.36, fov: 50 };\n    T.heroes.forEach((h, i) => {\n      const u = (T.t * .45 + i * .5) % 3, swing = u < .5 ? { spec: { a0: 1.4, a1: -1.6, z0: 12, z1: 8, reach: 7.5 }, phase: u < .15 ? 'wind' : 'active', u: u < .15 ? u / .15 : (u - .15) / .35 } : null;\n      h.facing = Math.atan2(Math.sin(a), Math.cos(a)) + (i ? -.5 : .5); h.anim = { attack: swing };\n    });\n    if (T.slime.grounded && (T.t % 1.6) < dt) T.slime.vz = 140;\n    T.slime.anim = { squash: T.slime.grounded ? 0 : .2 };\n    T.wisp.vz = (8 + 20 + Math.sin(T.t * 2) * 3 - T.wisp.z) * 4;\n    w.step(dt);\n  },\n  draw(r) {\n    title.world.draw(r);\n    const top = Math.max(10, Math.round(r.H * .1)), my = Math.round(r.H * .58);\n    titleMenu.y = my;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      veil(g, r, my - 14, .5);\n      E.font.title(g, 'my-3D2dge', r.W / 2, top, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347', '#e0662a'], depth: 3 });\n      E.font.title(g, '3D', r.W / 2, top + 36, { align: 'center', scale: 3, colors: ['#e8fcff', '#8af4ff', '#2aa0e0'], depth: 2, depthColor: '#14304a' });\n      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n    });\n    titleMenu.draw(r);\n    const dev = game.input.lastDevice, how = dev === 'touch' ? 'Tap a game to play it' : dev === 'gamepad' ? 'D-pad + ' + game.input.label('confirm') + '   ' + game.input.label('start') + ' menu' : 'Arrows + Enter or click   M mute';\n    r.text(how, r.W / 2, r.H - 26, '#b8b0d8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n  }\n};\n\n/* ---- GAME OVER and COURSE CLEAR: shared by every slice, over its world, frozen where it ended ---- */\nconst overMenu = new E.Menu(game, ['Retry', 'Title'], { y: 'center', onPick: i => game.go(i === 0 ? over.from : 'title') });\nlet over = { from: 'title', world: null, won: false, lines: [] };\nscenes.over = {\n  input: W3.INPUT,\n  enter(d) { over = Object.assign({ won: false, lines: [] }, d); overMenu.i = 0; A.music(over.won ? 'victory' : null); if (!over.won) A.sfx('die'); active = null; },\n  update(dt) { if (!overMenu.update(dt)) pickOnStart(overMenu); },\n  back() { game.go('title'); return true; },   // a phone's back gesture: to the title, not off the page\n  draw(r) {\n    if (over.world) over.world.draw(r);\n    const y = Math.round(r.H / 2) - 70; overMenu.y = y + 70 + over.lines.length * 10;\n    r.overlay(g => {\n      veil(g, r, 0, .6);\n      E.font.title(g, over.won ? over.title || 'CLEAR!' : 'GAME OVER', r.W / 2, y, { align: 'center', scale: 4, colors: over.won ? ['#fffbe8', '#ffe08a', '#ffb347'] : ['#ffe0e0', '#ff7a6a', '#c8202a'], depthColor: over.won ? '#3a2008' : '#3a0810' });\n      over.lines.forEach((l, i) => E.font.text(g, l, r.W / 2, y + 44 + i * 10, '#f0e6ff', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false }));\n    });\n    overMenu.draw(r);\n  }\n};\n/* ---- START: the boot (the 3D engine, then each slice's world, behind the boot screen), then the title menu, or a\n * slice named in the address (#platformer; #racing/vs: the slice's enter(data) gets { part }) ---- */\n// a 3D genre kit file holds one slice: the menu lists only the slices in this file\nfor (let i = SLICES.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) if (!scenes[SLICES[i].id]) SLICES.splice(i, 1);\ntitleMenu = menuOf(SLICES, { y: 0, room: 34, onPick: i => game.go(SLICES[i].id) });\nconst [first, part] = (location.hash || '').slice(1).split('/');\ngame.start({ scenes, scene: scenes[first] ? first : 'title', data: scenes[first] && part ? { part } : undefined, boot: { title: 'my-3D2dge 3D', steps: [\n  ['The 3D engine: three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3', () => W3.init(game)],\n  ...BOOT,\n  ['Building the shaders', () => { for (const w of W3.worlds) w.prepare(); }]\n] } });\nwindow.__game = { game, scenes, titleMenu, get title() { return title; } };   // for tests\n/* =============================== GAME END =============================== */\n/* =====================================================================================\n * SLICE 3  SHOOTER  (Apex Legends' movement and gunplay, without the multiplayer; first or third person). A badlands\n * two kilometres across, streamed as you go: golden grass that sways, red rock mesas in strata, dry riverbeds,\n * junipers and pines; six outposts joined by dirt roads, each with buildings to breach, containers, a watch tower with\n * a zipline and supply bins. MOVE: sprint, crouch, slide (downhill it speeds up), jump, vault low cover, mantle onto\n * ledges, climb walls, ladders, ziplines, kick doors in. FIGHT: a rifle and a shotgun (from the hip or down the\n * sights: recoil, spread, reloads), a punch with a lunge, frag grenades; raiders with shields hold five outposts, and\n * the drop point has a firing range. T switches first and third person.\n * THE 3D: the ground is a terrain (world terrain: a height and a color function, streamed in chunks for the physics\n * and the picture); the structures are one merged mesh over fixed blocks; grass is merged tufts that sway (TSL); trees\n * and rocks are shapes streamed by chunk. Every soldier is drawn by code with the pen on a procedural skeleton (feet\n * planted by IK on the ground under them, stepping round as it turns on the spot, a spine that leans and twists, hands\n * on the gun); first person draws its arms and guns with the overlay's pen, which never sinks into a wall. Muzzle\n * flashes and hits are stars of additive streaks facing the eye. A frame draws the moving things part way between the\n * last two steps (game.alpha) and turns the view by the newest mouse moves, so the motion is even at 60, 90, 144 or\n * 240 Hz; feet and hands blend into a new job instead of jumping. SHOOT.run(n): the proof's hash\n * ===================================================================================== */\nconst SHOOT = (() => {\n  const M = 16;   // engine units a metre\n  /* ---- TUNING: engine units (16 a metre) and seconds ---- */\n  const GRAV = 314, JUMP = 106, WALK = 68, RUN = 118, CROUCH = 40, ADS_WALK = 46, SLIDE_BOOST = 34, SLIDE_MAX = 182, SLIDE_DRAG = 62;\n  const RADIUS = 5, HALF = 9, HALF_CROUCH = 4, HALF_SLIDE = 1.5, EYE = 26, EYE_CROUCH = 17, EYE_SLIDE = 11;\n  const MANTLE_MAX = 40, VAULT_MAX = 19, CLIMB_SPEED = 96, CLIMB_TIME = .5, LADDER_SPEED = 76, ZIP_SPEED = 200;\n  const HP = 100, SHIELD = 100, FOV = 70;\n  const N2 = E.noise2, sstep = (a, b, x) => { const t = clamp((x - a) / (b - a), 0, 1); return t * t * (3 - 2 * t); };\n  const fbm = (x, y, o) => { let v = 0, a = 1, t = 0; for (let k = 0; k < o; k++) { v += a * N2(x, y); t += a; a *= .5; x = x * 2.03 + 17.1; y = y * 2.03 + 3.7; } return v / t; };\n\n  /* =====================================================================\n   * THE BADLANDS: the ground's height and color (metres inside, engine units out), the outposts and the roads\n   * ===================================================================== */\n  const HM = 2048, SIZE = HM * M;   // the map: 2,048 metres (32,768 units) square\n  // rasters every 4 m, made once at boot: the riverbeds, the roads (how much each flattens the ground, to what height,\n  // its dirt) and the outposts' pads\n  const RS = 4, RN = HM / RS + 1, RIVER = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADW = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADH = new Float32Array(RN * RN), ROADC = new Float32Array(RN * RN), PADW = new Float32Array(RN * RN), PADH = new Float32Array(RN * RN);\n  const rs = (A, m, n) => {   // a raster at (m, n) metres, bilinear\n    const gx = clamp(m / RS, 0, RN - 1.001), gy = clamp(n / RS, 0, RN - 1.001), i = gx | 0, j = gy | 0, u = gx - i, v = gy - j, k = j * RN + i;\n    return (A[k] * (1 - u) + A[k + 1] * u) * (1 - v) + (A[k + RN] * (1 - u) + A[k + RN + 1] * u) * v;\n  };\n  const riverAt = (m, n) => 1 - sstep(.014, .05, Math.abs(fbm(m / 610 + 5.1, n / 610 + 9.7, 3) - .5));\n  /** the land before roads and pads: broad hills, mesas in two tiers with ragged cliffs, riverbeds carved flat, small\n   *  swells, and a wall of cliffs round the map's edge */\n  function baseH(m, n) {\n    let h = (fbm(m / 420, n / 420, 4) - .5) * 70;\n    const f = fbm(m / 290 + 31.7, n / 290 + 11.3, 3) + (N2(m / 21, n / 21) - .5) * .045;\n    h += sstep(.575, .6, f) * 32 + sstep(.67, .69, f) * 18;\n    h -= rs(RIVER, m, n) * 7;\n    h += (N2(m / 33, n / 33) - .5) * 3.2 + (N2(m / 9.5, n / 9.5) - .5) * .7;\n    const e = Math.min(m, n, HM - m, HM - n); h += sstep(190, 30, e) * 140 + sstep(60, 0, e) * 60;\n    return h;\n  }\n  /** the terrain's height function (engine units): the land, flattened under the roads and the outposts */\n  function height(x, y) {\n    const m = x / M, n = y / M; let h = baseH(m, n);\n    const rw = rs(ROADW, m, n); if (rw > 0) h += (rs(ROADH, m, n) - h) * rw;\n    const pw = rs(PADW, m, n); if (pw > 0) h += (rs(PADH, m, n) - h) * pw;\n    return h * M;\n  }\n  /** the terrain's color function: golden grass patched olive and dry brown, pale sand in the riverbeds, dirt roads,\n   *  gravel pads, bare earth where it steepens (the rock in strata is the terrain's own, steeper still) */\n  function color(x, y, z, nz, out) {\n    const m = x / M, n = y / M, p = N2(m / 23, n / 23), q = N2(m / 71 + 9, n / 71 + 4), f = N2(m / 4.3, n / 4.3);\n    let r = 198, g = 170, b = 100;\n    if (q < .46) { const k = (.46 - q) / .46; r -= 46 * k; g -= 16 * k; b -= 12 * k; }\n    if (p > .6) { const k = (p - .6) / .4; r -= 20 * k; g -= 40 * k; b -= 18 * k; }\n    if (z > 30 * M) { const k = sstep(30 * M, 60 * M, z) * .5; r += 8 * k; g -= 14 * k; b -= 12 * k; }   // (the mesas' tops: redder, drier)\n    const mixTo = (k, R, G, B) => { r += (R - r) * k; g += (G - g) * k; b += (B - b) * k; };\n    mixTo(sstep(.9, .62, nz) * .8, 150, 112, 80);\n    mixTo(rs(RIVER, m, n) * .9, 214 + f * 20, 196 + f * 18, 158 + f * 14);\n    mixTo(sstep(.35, 1, rs(PADW, m, n)) * .8, 172 + f * 30 + p * 14, 150 + f * 24 + p * 8, 116 + f * 18);\n    mixTo(rs(ROADC, m, n) * .9, 160 + f * 18, 126 + f * 12, 92 + f * 10);\n    const k = .9 + f * .2; out[0] = r * k; out[1] = g * k; out[2] = b * k; return out;\n  }\n  /* the outposts: where each is meant to be, moved at boot to the flattest ground near there; DROP POINT (the start)\n     is the firing range. r: the pad's radius (metres) */\n  const OUTPOSTS = [\n    { id: 'drop', name: 'DROP POINT', at: [1030, 1560], r: 44 },\n    { id: 'relay', name: 'RELAY STATION', at: [610, 1010], r: 44 },\n    { id: 'salvage', name: 'SALVAGE YARD', at: [1480, 1230], r: 50 },\n    { id: 'pump', name: 'PUMP HOUSE', at: [1010, 600], r: 44 },\n    { id: 'ridge', name: 'RIDGE CAMP', at: [430, 1520], r: 40 },\n    { id: 'depot', name: 'THE DEPOT', at: [1580, 620], r: 50 }\n  ];\n  const OP = Object.fromEntries(OUTPOSTS.map(o => [o.id, o]));\n  const ROADS = [['drop', 'relay'], ['drop', 'salvage'], ['relay', 'pump'], ['pump', 'depot'], ['salvage', 'depot'], ['relay', 'ridge'], ['ridge', 'drop']];\n  const roads = [];   // each a list of [m, n, h] every 6 m\n  /** the cheapest way between two points over a 16 m grid (A*: distance, and much more for steep ground) */\n  function route(a, b, NH) {\n    const G = 128, S = HM / G, at = p => [clamp(Math.round(p[0] / S), 2, G - 3), clamp(Math.round(p[1] / S), 2, G - 3)];\n    const [ai, aj] = at(a), [bi, bj] = at(b), goal = bj * G + bi, cost = new Float32Array(G * G).fill(Infinity), from = new Int32Array(G * G).fill(-1), shut = new Uint8Array(G * G);\n    const hf = [], hk = [];   // a binary heap of (f, node)\n    const push = (f, k) => { let i = hf.length; hf.push(f); hk.push(k); while (i > 0) { const p = (i - 1) >> 1; if (hf[p] <= f) break; hf[i] = hf[p]; hk[i] = hk[p]; i = p; } hf[i] = f; hk[i] = k; };\n    const pop = () => { const top = hk[0], f = hf.pop(), k = hk.pop(); if (hf.length) { let i = 0; for (;;) { let c = 2 * i + 1; if (c >= hf.length) break; if (c + 1 < hf.length && hf[c + 1] < hf[c]) c++; if (hf[c] >= f) break; hf[i] = hf[c]; hk[i] = hk[c]; i = c; } hf[i] = f; hk[i] = k; } return top; };\n    cost[aj * G + ai] = 0; push(0, aj * G + ai);\n    while (hf.length) {\n      const k = pop(); if (shut[k]) continue; shut[k] = 1; if (k === goal) break;\n      const i = k % G, j = (k / G) | 0;\n      for (let dj = -1; dj <= 1; dj++) for (let di = -1; di <= 1; di++) {\n        const i2 = i + di, j2 = j + dj, k2 = j2 * G + i2; if ((!di && !dj) || i2 < 2 || j2 < 2 || i2 > G - 3 || j2 > G - 3 || shut[k2]) continue;\n        const d = Math.hypot(di, dj) * S, sl = Math.abs(NH[k2] - NH[k]) / d, c = cost[k] + d * (1 + 45 * sl * sl + (sl > .28 ? 80 : 0));\n        if (c < cost[k2]) { cost[k2] = c; from[k2] = k; push(c + Math.hypot(i2 - bi, j2 - bj) * S, k2); }\n      }\n    }\n    const path = []; for (let k = goal; k >= 0; k = from[k]) path.push([(k % G) * S, ((k / G) | 0) * S]);\n    path.reverse(); path[0] = [a[0], a[1]]; path[path.length - 1] = [b[0], b[1]]; return path;\n  }\n  /** the boot's planning: the riverbeds, the outposts on flat ground, their pads, the roads routed, smoothed and laid */\n  function planLand() {\n    for (let j = 0; j < RN; j++) for (let i = 0; i < RN; i++) RIVER[j * RN + i] = riverAt(i * RS, j * RS);\n    for (const o of OUTPOSTS) {\n      let best = null;\n      for (let k = 0; k < 110; k++) {\n        const a = k * 2.399, rr = Math.sqrt(k) * 14, m = o.at[0] + Math.cos(a) * rr, n = o.at[1] + Math.sin(a) * rr, h0 = baseH(m, n);\n        let dev = 0; for (let q = 0; q < 8; q++) { const b = q * TAU / 8, c = Math.cos(b), s = Math.sin(b); dev += Math.abs(baseH(m + c * o.r, n + s * o.r) - h0) + Math.abs(baseH(m + c * o.r * .55, n + s * o.r * .55) - h0); }\n        const score = dev + rr * .03 + rs(RIVER, m, n) * 60; if (!best || score < best[0]) best = [score, m, n, h0];\n      }\n      [, o.m, o.n, o.h] = best; o.x = o.m * M; o.y = o.n * M; o.z = o.h * M;\n    }\n    const G = 128, S = HM / G, NH = new Float32Array(G * G);\n    for (let j = 0; j < G; j++) for (let i = 0; i < G; i++) NH[j * G + i] = baseH(i * S, j * S);\n    const best = new Float32Array(RN * RN).fill(1e9);\n    for (const [a, b] of ROADS) {\n      let p = route([OP[a].m, OP[a].n], [OP[b].m, OP[b].n], NH);\n      for (let it = 0; it < 3; it++) { const q = [p[0]]; for (let i = 0; i < p.length - 1; i++) { const u = p[i], v = p[i + 1]; q.push([u[0] * .75 + v[0] * .25, u[1] * .75 + v[1] * .25], [u[0] * .25 + v[0] * .75, u[1] * .25 + v[1] * .75]); } q.push(p[p.length - 1]); p = q; }   // (Chaikin's corners cut)\n      const pts = [p[0]]; let acc = 0;\n      for (let i = 1; i < p.length; i++) { const d = Math.hypot(p[i][0] - p[i - 1][0], p[i][1] - p[i - 1][1]); acc += d; if (acc >= 6 || i === p.length - 1) { pts.push(p[i]); acc = 0; } }\n      const raw = pts.map(q => baseH(q[0], q[1])), road = pts.map((q, i) => { let s = 0, w = 0; for (let k = -5; k <= 5; k++) { const v = raw[clamp(i + k, 0, raw.length - 1)]; s += v; w++; } return [q[0], q[1], s / w]; });\n      roads.push(road);\n      for (let i = 0; i < road.length - 1; i++) {   // laid into the rasters: the flattening within 10 m, the dirt within 5.5 m\n        const [x0, y0, h0] = road[i], [x1, y1, h1] = road[i + 1], dx = x1 - x0, dy = y1 - y0, L2 = dx * dx + dy * dy || 1;\n        for (let cj = Math.max(0, Math.floor((Math.min(y0, y1) - 14) / RS)); cj <= Math.min(RN - 1, Math.ceil((Math.max(y0, y1) + 14) / RS)); cj++)\n          for (let ci = Math.max(0, Math.floor((Math.min(x0, x1) - 14) / RS)); ci <= Math.min(RN - 1, Math.ceil((Math.max(x0, x1) + 14) / RS)); ci++) {\n            const px = ci * RS, py = cj * RS, t = clamp(((px - x0) * dx + (py - y0) * dy) / L2, 0, 1), d = Math.hypot(px - x0 - dx * t, py - y0 - dy * t), k = cj * RN + ci;\n            if (d < 14 && d < best[k]) { best[k] = d; ROADH[k] = h0 + (h1 - h0) * t; ROADW[k] = sstep(10, 4.5, d); }\n            ROADC[k] = Math.max(ROADC[k], sstep(5.5, 2.5, d));\n          }\n      }\n    }\n    for (const o of OUTPOSTS) {   // the pads: flat at the outpost's height within r, easing out over 30 m\n      for (let cj = Math.max(0, Math.floor((o.n - o.r - 36) / RS)); cj <= Math.min(RN - 1, Math.ceil((o.n + o.r + 36) / RS)); cj++)\n        for (let ci = Math.max(0, Math.floor((o.m - o.r - 36) / RS)); ci <= Math.min(RN - 1, Math.ceil((o.m + o.r + 36) / RS)); ci++) {\n          const d = Math.hypot(ci * RS - o.m, cj * RS - o.n), k = cj * RN + ci, w = sstep(o.r + 30, o.r, d);\n          if (d < o.r + 36 && (w > PADW[k] || (!PADW[k] && !PADH[k]))) { PADW[k] = w; PADH[k] = o.h; }\n        }\n    }\n  }\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |''^### |Things to know'\"' engine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md engine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md && sed -n '1920,2090p' src/30-shooter.js\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## |''^### |Things to know'\"' engine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md engine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md && sed -n '1920,2090p' src/30-shooter.js\"","aggregated_output":"engine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:9:## Use one\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:34:## The core library\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:46:## Materials on surfaces\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:84:## Write one\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:116:### Worked entries\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:135:## Make one: the recipe\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md:155:## Limits\nengine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md:18:## How it fits the 2D engine\nengine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md:101:## The kits\nengine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md:169:## Checks\nengine-repo/docs/ENGINE-3D.md:184:## Things to know\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:9:## Quick start (a complete game)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:40:## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:53:## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:70:## Rules\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:79:## Common mistakes (check these first)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:90:## Game\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:106:## Scenes (title, play, game over)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:117:## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:133:## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:140:## Input: `game.input`\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:150:## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:159:## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:168:## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:174:## Levels\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:186:## Movement and physics\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:204:## Characters\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:220:## Effects and lighting\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:226:## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:266:## More: animation and examples outside this card\nengine-repo/dist/handoff/API.md:290:## Before you hand the game back\n  /* =====================================================================\n   * THE STEP, THE FRAME, A FRESH START, THE PROOF\n   * ===================================================================== */\n  const { start, pause, confirm, cancel } = E.Input.DEFAULT;\n  const KEYS = { up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n    jump: ['Space', 'Pad0'], crouch: ['KeyC', 'Pad1'], sprint: ['ShiftLeft', 'ShiftRight', 'Pad10'], fire: ['Mouse0', 'KeyJ', 'Pad7'], aim: ['Mouse2', 'KeyK', 'Pad6'],\n    reload: ['KeyR', 'Pad2'], use: ['KeyE', 'KeyF', 'Pad2'], melee: ['KeyV', 'Pad11'], grenade: ['KeyG', 'Pad4'], swap: ['KeyQ', 'Digit1', 'Digit2', 'Pad3'], view: ['KeyT', 'Pad5'],\n    start, pause, confirm, cancel };\n  const TOUCH = ['use', 'melee', 'swap', 'crouch', 'jump', 'aim', 'fire'], TOUCH_LABELS = { use: 'USE', melee: 'HIT', swap: 'SWAP', crouch: 'DUCK', jump: 'JUMP', aim: 'AIM', fire: 'FIRE' };\n  /** one step of the game */\n  function step(dt, I) {\n    if (!(dt > 0)) { ip.still = true; world.step(0); return; }   // (time stopped, timeScale 0: nothing moves)\n    keepPrev(dt); I0 = I; S.time += dt;\n    if (S.alive && !S.won) { look(dt, I); move(dt, I); actions(dt, I); bump(); }\n    else { hero.vx = approach(hero.vx, 0, 600 * dt); hero.vy = approach(hero.vy, 0, 600 * dt); S.act = null; S.ads = false; }\n    S.near = S.alive ? nearUse() : null;\n    streamRaiders(); for (const e of raiders.slice()) raiderStep(e, dt);\n    stepDoors(dt); stepLoot(dt); stepNades(dt);\n    streamScatter(world, hero.x, hero.y);\n    // footsteps, timers\n    const sp = Math.hypot(hero.vx, hero.vy);\n    if (hero.grounded && (S.move === 'stand' || S.move === 'crouch') && sp > 20) { const was = S.stepPh; S.stepPh += sp / ((16 + sp * .3) / 2) * dt; if (Math.floor(was) !== Math.floor(S.stepPh)) A.sfx('step', { vol: S.crouch ? .3 : S.sprint ? 1 : .7 }); }\n    S.hurtT = Math.max(0, S.hurtT - dt); for (const h of S.hitDirs) h.t -= dt; S.hitDirs = S.hitDirs.filter(h => h.t > 0);\n    for (const n of S.nums) n.t += dt; S.nums = S.nums.filter(n => n.t < 1.1); if (S.mark) S.mark.t -= dt;\n    for (const f of S.feed) f.t -= dt; S.feed = S.feed.filter(f => f.t > 0); if (S.banner) S.banner.t -= dt;\n    if (OP.ridge.fire && (S.time * 9) % 1 < dt * 9 && Math.hypot(OP.ridge.x - hero.x, OP.ridge.y - hero.y) < 120 * M) P.fire(OP.ridge.fire[0], OP.ridge.fire[1], OP.ridge.fire[2] + 1, 2, { size: 3, speed: 14 });\n    if (hero.fell) { const s = atP(OP.drop.P, 0, 14); hero.place(s[0], s[1]); }\n    world.step(dt);\n    camStep(dt);\n  }\n  let lastDraw = null, lastReal = null, lights = null, drawT = 0;   // drawT: the clock of the frame drawn (between the last two steps)\n  /* the steps run 120 times a second and a display 60, 90, 144 or 240 times: a frame shows the moving things part way\n   * from where the step before left them to where the last one did (game.alpha), so motion is as even at any rate */\n  const ip = { h: null, cam: null, eye: 0, adsB: 0, ph: 0, clr: 0, dt: 1 / 120, real: -1, still: false };\n  function keepPrev(dt) {\n    Object.assign(ip, { h: [hero.x, hero.y, hero.z], cam: S.cam, eye: S.eye, adsB: S.adsB, ph: S.stepPh, clr: S.camClr, dt, real: game.real, still: false });\n    for (const e of raiders) e.ip = [e.a.x, e.a.y, e.a.z];\n    for (const g of nades) g.ip = [g.x, g.y, g.z];\n  }\n  /** a point part way from where it was before the step to where it is (al: the frame's alpha); one that jumped (a respawn) is where it is */\n  const between = (was, x, y, z, al) => !was || Math.abs(x - was[0]) + Math.abs(y - was[1]) + Math.abs(z - was[2]) > 40 ? [x, y, z] : [lerp(was[0], x, al), lerp(was[1], y, al), lerp(was[2], z, al)];\n  /** the player's body follows the player (its heading along the run at a sprint, else with the view) */\n  function syncBody(dt, hp) {\n    const b = pb, h = hero;\n    // (a shot from the hip shoulders the gun for a moment, so the gun and its flash are seen in third person)\n    Object.assign(b, { x: hp[0], y: hp[1], z: hp[2], vx: h.vx, vy: h.vy, vz: h.vz, grounded: h.grounded, sprint: S.sprint, ads: S.ads || S.time - S.lastShot < .5, low: S.view === 'third', weapon: S.cur, act: S.act, actT: S.actT, reloadDur: S.actDur, reloadEmpty: S.reloadEmpty, aimYaw: S.yaw, aimPitch: S.pitch });\n    if (S.alive) b.move = (S.move === 'stand' || S.move === 'crouch') && !h.grounded ? 'air' : S.move;\n    const want = S.sprint && Math.hypot(h.vx, h.vy) > 40 && S.view === 'third' ? Math.atan2(h.vy, h.vx) : S.yaw; b.yaw = E.approachAng(b.yaw, want, dt * 10);\n    const R = S.act === 'reload' ? reloadCurve(S.cur, S.actT, S.actDur, S.reloadEmpty) : null;\n    b.gun = { mag: R ? R.mag : 0, bolt: R ? R.bolt : 0, pump: S.cur === 'shotgun' ? pumpCurve(S.pumpT) : 0, flash: S.flash, magP: null, shellP: null };\n    if (b.dead) b.dead.t += dt;\n  }\n  function syncRaider(e, dt, al) {\n    const a = e.a, b = e.b, p = between(e.ip, a.x, a.y, a.z, al);\n    Object.assign(b, { x: p[0], y: p[1], z: p[2], vx: a.vx, vy: a.vy, vz: a.vz, grounded: a.grounded, aimYaw: e.yaw, aimPitch: e.pitch, ads: e.sees && e.state === 'combat', low: !e.dummy && !(e.sees && e.state === 'combat'), flash: (e.hitNew ? (e.hitReal = performance.now() / 1000, e.hitNew = false, 1) : performance.now() / 1000 - (e.hitReal ?? -9) < .025) ? 1 : 0 });   // (two frames white, on the clock: the hit-stop doesn't stretch it)\n    if (e.alive) b.move = !a.grounded ? 'air' : e.crouch ? 'crouch' : 'stand';\n    b.yaw = E.approachAng(b.yaw, e.yaw, dt * 8); b.sprint = Math.hypot(a.vx, a.vy) > 64;\n    b.gun = { mag: 0, bolt: 0, pump: 0, flash: e.flash };\n  }\n  /** each frame, before the world draws: the grass and tracers round the camera, the soldiers posed and drawn, the\n   *  outposts' working parts, the lights, and in first person the arms and the gun */\n  function onDraw(w) {\n    if (!S) return;\n    // (a frame after a step that didn't run the game, paused or in a hit-stop, shows the last step as it is)\n    const al = ip.still || ip.real !== game.real || game.hitstop > 0 || !ip.h ? 1 : clamp(game.alpha, 0, 1), hp = between(ip.h, hero.x, hero.y, hero.z, al);\n    drawT = w.time - (1 - al) * ip.dt;\n    const dt = clamp(drawT - (lastDraw ?? drawT), 0, .05); lastDraw = drawT;\n    let cam = S.cam || w.camera.fixed;\n    if (S.cam) {   // the camera where the frame is, turned by the newest mouse moves at once (the next step takes them)\n      const live = S.alive && !S.won, m = w.camera.mouse, k = live ? lookK() : 0, pc = ip.cam || cam;\n      const yaw = cam.yaw + m[0] * k, pitch = clamp(cam.pitch - m[1] * k, -1.5, 1.5), roll = lerp(pc.roll, cam.roll, al), fov = lerp(pc.fov, cam.fov, al);\n      let p = between(pc && [pc.x, pc.y, pc.z], cam.x, cam.y, cam.z, al);\n      if (S.view === 'third' && live) p = thirdCam(hp[0], hp[1], hp[2], lerp(ip.eye, S.eye, al), lerp(ip.adsB, S.adsB, al), lerp(ip.ph, S.stepPh, al), yaw, pitch, lerp(ip.clr, S.camClr, al)).p;\n      cam = Object.assign({}, cam, { x: p[0], y: p[1], z: p[2], yaw, pitch, roll, fov }); w.camera.pose = Object.assign({ ortho: false }, cam);\n    }\n    fx.cam = [cam.x, cam.y, cam.z];\n    drawGrass(w, cam.x, cam.y); grass.uT.value = drawT; grass.uP.value.set(hp[0] / M, hp[2] / M, hp[1] / M); drawTracers(dt);\n    const pen = w.pen; pen.at();\n    syncBody(dt, hp);\n    if (S.view === 'third' || !S.alive) { pose(w, pb, dt); if (pb.gun.mag === 1) pb.gun.magP = add(pb.J.hands[0], pb.G.u, 2.1); drawSoldier(pen, pb); }\n    for (const e of raiders) {\n      const d = Math.hypot(e.a.x - cam.x, e.a.y - cam.y); if (d > 320 * M || !w.camera.sees(e.a.x, e.a.y, e.a.z, 40)) continue;\n      if (S.view === 'first' && e.alive && d < 8 && cam.z > e.a.z && cam.z < e.a.z + 32 * e.b.k) continue;   // (a body the eye is inside isn't drawn)\n      syncRaider(e, dt, al); e.b.visible = d < 110 * M; pose(w, e.b, dt); drawSoldier(pen, e.b);\n      if (e.flash > .6 && e.b.G) w.glow(...at(e.b.G, 12.8, .55), 1.2, '#ffc870', { light: true, core: '#fff4d0' });\n    }\n    drawWorks(pen, cam.x, cam.y, al);\n    const L = lights, F = frameYP([cam.x, cam.y, cam.z], S.yaw, S.pitch), mz = muzzlePoint(F);\n    Object.assign(L.muzzle, { x: mz[0], y: mz[1], z: mz[2], on: S.flash > .6, power: (S.view === 'third' ? 11 : 6) * S.flash, reach: S.view === 'third' ? 160 : 100 });   // (the shot's own frame only: no strobe)\n    if (S.boom && S.boom.t > 0) { Object.assign(L.boom, { x: S.boom.x, y: S.boom.y, z: S.boom.z + 20, on: true, power: 90 * S.boom.t / .35 }); S.boom.t -= dt; } else L.boom.on = false;\n    const fire = OP.ridge.fire; if (fire) { const fl = .85 + Math.sin(drawT * 13) * .08 + Math.sin(drawT * 29) * .06; Object.assign(L.fire, { x: fire[0], y: fire[1], z: fire[2] + 10, on: Math.hypot(fire[0] - cam.x, fire[1] - cam.y) < 140 * M, power: 18 * fl }); w.glow(fire[0], fire[1], fire[2] + 3, 2.6 * fl, '#ff9a3a', { core: '#fff0b0' }); }\n    for (const o of OUTPOSTS) if (o.beacon && (w.time % 1.6) < .8) w.glow(...o.beacon, 4, '#ff3a2a', { core: '#ffd0c0' });\n    w.overlay.on = S.view === 'first' && S.alive;\n    if (w.overlay.on) { w.overlay.camera.fov = lerp(54, 44, ease(S.adsB)); drawViewModel(w.overlay.pen, dt, cam); }\n    const now = performance.now() / 1000, rdt = clamp(now - (lastReal ?? now), 0, .05); lastReal = now;   // (hits' stars run on the clock: a hit-stop freezes the world, not the spark)\n    for (const st of fx.stars) {\n      const list = st.ov ? fx.flashes.ov : fx.flashes.world; if (list.length >= FL_MAX) continue;\n      if (st.v) { const u = st.t / st.life, q = add(st.p, st.v, st.t); q[2] -= (st.ov ? 450 : 900) * st.t * st.t; list.push({ p: q, f: st.f, s: st.s * (1 - u * .5), heat: .7 * (1 - u * .7), seed: st.seed + Math.floor(st.t * 60), pal: st.pal, thin: true }); }\n      // (the first frame is anything under half a frame old: a frame of clock time can compare as a hair under 1/60)\n      else { const first = st.t < .5 / 60; list.push({ p: st.p, f: st.f, s: st.s * (first ? 1.5 : .85), heat: first ? 1 : .5, seed: st.seed, pal: st.pal, thin: !first }); }\n    }\n    for (const st of fx.stars) st.t += rdt;\n    fx.stars = fx.stars.filter(st => st.t < (st.life || 1.5 / 60));\n    drawFlashes(fx.flW, fx.flashes.world, fx.cam); drawFlashes(fx.flO, fx.flashes.ov, [0, 0, 0]);\n  }\n  /** a fresh run: the world reset, the structures' blocks, doors shut, bins full, crews home, the player at the drop\n   *  point facing the range, the scatter round them at once */\n  function reset(seed = 1) {\n    world.reset(); rnd = E.rng(seed);\n    raiders.length = loot.length = nades.length = 0; placed.clear(); fx.tracers.length = fx.stars.length = 0; lastDraw = null; ip.h = ip.cam = null;\n    for (const s of solids) world.block(s);\n    for (const d of doors) Object.assign(d, { state: 'shut', ang: 0, want: 0, block: null, deb: null });\n    for (const b of bins) Object.assign(b, { open: 0, want: 0, used: false });\n    for (const sl of spawns) { sl.dead = false; sl.e = null; }\n    for (const o of OUTPOSTS) { o.spawned = false; o.left = spawns.filter(s => s.op === o.id).length; }\n    S = newState(); const P0 = OP.drop.P, s0 = atP(P0, 0, 14); S.yaw = P0.yaw - Math.PI / 2;\n    hero = world.hero({ x: s0[0], y: s0[1], r: RADIUS, half: HALF, visible: false, shadow: false, slope: 48, step: 5, snap: 5 });\n    pb = body('player'); pb.yaw = S.yaw;\n    for (const d of dummies) spawnRaider(Object.assign({ dummy: true, op: 'drop' }, d));\n    streamScatter(world, hero.x, hero.y, 1e9);\n    world.camera.set('fixed'); world.camera.follow(S.focus); camStep(0);\n  }\n  const I = { move: [0, 0], mouse: [0, 0], stick2: null, pressed: (a, w) => game.input.buffered(a, w), use: a => game.input.consume(a), down: a => game.input.down(a) };\n  /** the proof: a scripted run from the drop point (moving, sprinting, a slide, jumps, bursts at the range, a punch, a\n   *  swap, a reload, aiming), n steps of 1/120 s; returns the world's hash */\n  function run(n = 600) {\n    reset(3); let i = 0;\n    const c = { move: [0, -1], mouse: [0, 0], stick2: null, use() {},\n      pressed: a => (a === 'jump' && i % 150 === 40) || (a === 'crouch' && i === 190) || (a === 'melee' && i === 330) || (a === 'swap' && i === 400) || (a === 'fire' && i > 420 && i % 50 === 0) || (a === 'reload' && i === 560),\n      down: a => (a === 'sprint' && i < 200) || (a === 'fire' && i > 100 && i < 330 && i % 60 < 30) || (a === 'aim' && i > 440) || (a === 'crouch' && i > 190 && i < 230) };\n    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) { c.move = [Math.sin(i / 70) * .5, -1]; c.mouse = [Math.sin(i / 50) * 3, Math.cos(i / 80) * 1.2]; step(1 / 120, c); }\n    return world.hash([S.kills, S.ammo.rifle[0], S.ammo.shotgun[0], S.hp, S.shield, raiders.length, Math.round(S.yaw * 1000)]);\n  }\n  /* ---- a phone: a finger on the look side drags the view (the move stick is on the other) ---- */\n  function touchLook() {\n    const cv = game.screen.canvas; if (!cv || typeof document === 'undefined') return;\n    const ids = new Map();\n    cv.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { if (e.pointerType === 'mouse' || active !== world || game.paused) return; const r = cv.getBoundingClientRect(), right = e.clientX - r.left > r.width * .5; if (right === (game.input.stickSide === 'right')) return; ids.set(e.pointerId, [e.clientX, e.clientY]); });\n    cv.addEventListener('pointermove', e => { const p = ids.get(e.pointerId); if (!p || active !== world) return; world.camera.mouse[0] += (e.clientX - p[0]) * 2.4; world.camera.mouse[1] += (e.clientY - p[1]) * 2.4; p[0] = e.clientX; p[1] = e.clientY; });\n    const up = e => ids.delete(e.pointerId); addEventListener('pointerup', up); addEventListener('pointercancel', up);\n  }\n  BOOT.push(['The badlands: land, roads and outposts', () => { for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(SOUNDS)) A.define(k, v); planLand(); layout(); }]);\n  BOOT.push(['The open world', () => {\n    world = new W3(game, { terrain: { size: SIZE, cell: 32, chunk: 32, height, color, far: 17000, physics: 1400, detail: 1.2, rock: { colors: ['#a8644a', '#c47e5a', '#8e523c', '#d0946a', '#b06e50', '#7a4632', '#c8885e'], band: 46, slope: [.34, .52] }, speckle: .2, mottle: .34 },\n      sky: { top: '#3d6fb8', horizon: '#f2dcb4', ground: '#b49070', sun: '#fff0c8', haze: .3 }, fog: { color: '#ead4b0', near: 2200, far: 19000 },\n      ambient: ['#c4d4ee', '#8a6a48', 1.55], sun: { color: '#fff0d8', intensity: 3.1, dir: [-.55, .4, -.62], area: 1150, map: 2048 },\n      torchLights: 0, glowLights: 4, lights: 3, overlay: { fov: 58 }, camera: { mode: 'fixed', capture: true, near: 1.2 }, res: 'balanced', gravity: GRAV, onDraw });\n    structureMesh(world); grassMeshes(world); fxMeshes(world);\n    lights = { muzzle: world.light({ color: '#ffc870', reach: 220, power: 0 }), boom: world.light({ color: '#ff9a4a', reach: 700, power: 0 }), fire: world.light({ color: '#ff8a3a', reach: 170, power: 0 }) };\n    reset(1); touchLook();\n  }]);\n  return {\n    view: 'iso', input: KEYS, pausable: true, touch: TOUCH,\n    enter() { reset(1); active = world; A.music(null); game.input.touchButtons(TOUCH, { labels: TOUCH_LABELS }); },\n    update(dt) {\n      I.move = game.input.move(); world.camera.takeMouse(I.mouse); I.stick2 = game.input.padAim;\n      step(dt, I);\n      const inp = game.input; inp.touchSet('use', S.near ? 'USE' : null, !!S.near); inp.touchSet('melee', S.near && S.near.kick ? 'KICK' : null, !!(S.near && S.near.kick) || raiders.some(e => e.alive && Math.hypot(e.a.x - hero.x, e.a.y - hero.y) < 5 * M));\n    },\n    draw(r) { world.draw(r); r.overlay(g => hud(g, r)); },\n    get world() { return world; }, get hero() { return hero; }, get state() { return S; }, get raiders() { return raiders; },\n    /** the player's soldier (b.J: its joints, posed each frame it is drawn) and the first-person arms and gun (vm.F: the\n     *  gun's frame in the eyes' space, vm.L, vm.R: the hands), for tools that measure the motion */\n    get player() { return pb; }, get viewModel() { return vm; }, get outposts() { return OUTPOSTS; }, reset, run,\n    /** the soldier's rig, for a sheet of its poses (tools, tests): body(look), pose(world, b, dt), draw(pen, b) */\n    rig: { body, pose, draw: drawSoldier, onDraw }\n  };\n})();\nscenes.shooter = SHOOT;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
