{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('src/compat.html');p.write_text('''<script>\n// Three r182's WebGL fallback imports standard GPU flags even without navigator.gpu.\nfor(const [key,value] of Object.entries({GPUShaderStage:{VERTEX:1,FRAGMENT:2,COMPUTE:4},GPUBufferUsage:{MAP_READ:1,MAP_WRITE:2,COPY_SRC:4,COPY_DST:8,INDEX:16,VERTEX:32,UNIFORM:64,STORAGE:128,INDIRECT:256,QUERY_RESOLVE:512},GPUTextureUsage:{COPY_SRC:1,COPY_DST:2,TEXTURE_BINDING:4,STORAGE_BINDING:8,RENDER_ATTACHMENT:16},GPUMapMode:{READ:1,WRITE:2},GPUColorWrite:{RED:1,GREEN:2,BLUE:4,ALPHA:8,ALL:15}}))if(typeof globalThis[key]==='undefined')globalThis[key]=value;\n</script>''')\np=Path('build.mjs');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"<script>window.__answers=\\\", \\\"\"'${rd('\"'src/compat.html','utf8')}<script>window.__answers=\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('ENGINE-CHANGES.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'- Page compatibility prelude: provide standard WebGPU bit-flag constants only when missing, so three r182 can import its WebGL fallback in Firefox without WebGPU. No renderer or hardware API is emulated.\\\\n')\np=Path('test/ISSUES.md');p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\\\\n20. Firefox rendered boot: three r182 referenced missing WebGPU flag globals during import even on the WebGL path. Supply only absent standard flag constants before the module imports. Critical cross-browser boot defect. Firefox rendering on this headless machine also requires its own Xvfb display, which is test setup rather than a game defect.\\\\n')\nPY\nnode build.mjs\npython3 test/run.py --suite core\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
