{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_139","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib,os\nroot=Path.cwd().parent\nreport=json.loads(Path('test/final-report.json').read_text())\nassert len(report)==78 and all(x['pass'] for x in report)\nhtml=root/(Path.cwd().name+'.html');data=html.read_text();answers=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nassert data.split('<script>',1)[1].split('</script>',1)[0]==Path('hub/session.js').read_text()\nassert '27 distinct' in answers['testingFeedback'][0] and answers['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert 'third-party-licenses' in data\nassert not Path('engine-repo').exists()\npackage=json.loads(Path('test/package-report.json').read_text());package.update(bytes=html.stat().st_size,sha256=hashlib.sha256(html.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),testsPassed=78,testsFailed=0);Path('test/package-report.json').write_text(json.dumps(package,indent=2))\np=root/'PROGRESS.md';s=p.read_text();line='# Dead Sea Sigh — build progress\\\\n';s=s.replace(line,line+'\\\\n**Status: COMPLETE.** All milestones M0–M11 are finished. The final combined command passed **78/78 checks**, including the non-cheating opening, all contracts and three endings, WebKit mobile/tablet UI, controller navigation/paused About, rendered multiplayer pickup/banking/melee/fire, all five hub conformance scenarios, WebGPU, and matching WebGL/WebGPU replay hashes.\\\\n\\\\nDeliverables: the root standalone HTML and \"'`exit-interview.json`. All required feedback is also embedded in About/Credits. The development folder contains the build source, README, license notices, 78-check final report and inspected screenshots. The engine checkout and scratch diagnostics have been removed. No further work is pending.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe remainder is the chronological build record.\\\\n',1)\ns+='\\\\n## Complete\\\\n- Final command: \"'`python3 test/run.py` — **78/78 checks passed; 0 failures**. Detailed results: dev-folder `test/final-report.json`.'\"\\\\n- Corrected issues: 27, including 11 classed critical; environmental terminations and test-fixture timing errors excluded.\\\\n- Final root HTML is self-contained, includes required feedback and third-party licenses, and preserves the session client unmodified. JSON validates.\\\\n- Actual iOS Safari/physical pad/TV/human listening were unavailable; WebKit and device/pad/audio stand-ins were used. Firefox simulation/replay passed; rendered Firefox was unavailable in this headless environment.\\\\n- Final package size: '+str(package['bytes'])+' bytes. SHA-256: \"'`'\"'+package['sha256']+'\"'`.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\n# All local test servers are scoped to this dev folder; report any unexpected remaining owned server.\nremaining=[]\nfor proc in Path('/proc').iterdir():\n if not proc.name.isdigit():continue\n try:\n  if (proc/'cwd').resolve()\"'!=Path.cwd()/'\"'hub':continue\n  args=(proc/'cmdline').read_bytes().replace(b'\\\\0',b' ').decode(errors='replace')\n  if '-m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1' in args:remaining.append(int(proc.name))\n except OSError:pass\nassert not remaining,remaining\nprint(json.dumps({'tests':'78/78 passed','bytes':package['bytes'],'sha256':package['sha256'],'interview':'valid','engineCheckout':'removed','ownedTestServers':remaining}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_139","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,hashlib,os\nroot=Path.cwd().parent\nreport=json.loads(Path('test/final-report.json').read_text())\nassert len(report)==78 and all(x['pass'] for x in report)\nhtml=root/(Path.cwd().name+'.html');data=html.read_text();answers=json.loads((root/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\nassert data.split('<script>',1)[1].split('</script>',1)[0]==Path('hub/session.js').read_text()\nassert '27 distinct' in answers['testingFeedback'][0] and answers['sourceInformation']['usage']=='added on import'\nassert 'third-party-licenses' in data\nassert not Path('engine-repo').exists()\npackage=json.loads(Path('test/package-report.json').read_text());package.update(bytes=html.stat().st_size,sha256=hashlib.sha256(html.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),testsPassed=78,testsFailed=0);Path('test/package-report.json').write_text(json.dumps(package,indent=2))\np=root/'PROGRESS.md';s=p.read_text();line='# Dead Sea Sigh — build progress\\\\n';s=s.replace(line,line+'\\\\n**Status: COMPLETE.** All milestones M0–M11 are finished. The final combined command passed **78/78 checks**, including the non-cheating opening, all contracts and three endings, WebKit mobile/tablet UI, controller navigation/paused About, rendered multiplayer pickup/banking/melee/fire, all five hub conformance scenarios, WebGPU, and matching WebGL/WebGPU replay hashes.\\\\n\\\\nDeliverables: the root standalone HTML and \"'`exit-interview.json`. All required feedback is also embedded in About/Credits. The development folder contains the build source, README, license notices, 78-check final report and inspected screenshots. The engine checkout and scratch diagnostics have been removed. No further work is pending.'\"\\\\n\\\\nThe remainder is the chronological build record.\\\\n',1)\ns+='\\\\n## Complete\\\\n- Final command: \"'`python3 test/run.py` — **78/78 checks passed; 0 failures**. Detailed results: dev-folder `test/final-report.json`.'\"\\\\n- Corrected issues: 27, including 11 classed critical; environmental terminations and test-fixture timing errors excluded.\\\\n- Final root HTML is self-contained, includes required feedback and third-party licenses, and preserves the session client unmodified. JSON validates.\\\\n- Actual iOS Safari/physical pad/TV/human listening were unavailable; WebKit and device/pad/audio stand-ins were used. Firefox simulation/replay passed; rendered Firefox was unavailable in this headless environment.\\\\n- Final package size: '+str(package['bytes'])+' bytes. SHA-256: \"'`'\"'+package['sha256']+'\"'`.'\"\\\\n'\np.write_text(s)\n# All local test servers are scoped to this dev folder; report any unexpected remaining owned server.\nremaining=[]\nfor proc in Path('/proc').iterdir():\n if not proc.name.isdigit():continue\n try:\n  if (proc/'cwd').resolve()\"'!=Path.cwd()/'\"'hub':continue\n  args=(proc/'cmdline').read_bytes().replace(b'\\\\0',b' ').decode(errors='replace')\n  if '-m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1' in args:remaining.append(int(proc.name))\n except OSError:pass\nassert not remaining,remaining\nprint(json.dumps({'tests':'78/78 passed','bytes':package['bytes'],'sha256':package['sha256'],'interview':'valid','engineCheckout':'removed','ownedTestServers':remaining}))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"tests\": \"78/78 passed\", \"bytes\": 4901933, \"sha256\": \"e3851b4ca65dad6a89c46025b9a575f39a5c0913dfe870adae1fe01570838038\", \"interview\": \"valid\", \"engineCheckout\": \"removed\", \"ownedTestServers\": []}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_140","type":"agent_message","text":"Built [**Dead Sea Sigh**](</home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261105-053720__x448574/work/Dead Sea Sigh-Far Cry 2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-053720.html>). Open the self-contained HTML in a browser. **78/78 checks passed.**\n\n[Progress log](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261105-053720__x448574/work/PROGRESS.md) · [Required feedback JSON](/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261105-053720__x448574/work/exit-interview.json)\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-05 05:37:20. Inspired by Far Cry 2; plan: `PLAN.md`. First-person open-world survival shooter. Tech: my-3D2dge v0.88.0/World3D, three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3, esbuild 0.28.2. Native outlined low-poly art, pixel UI, procedural IK and keyframed hands. Code-generated music, effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%. AI Hub supports 1–4 players; solo Salvage Rights has AI rivals. Research used the supplied plan and engine/hub documentation. Environment: Codex CLI, headless Linux. Model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max. Usage: **added on import**.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** Found and fixed 27 issues, including 11 classified critical. The full campaign bot was most helpful; the earliest page-error-only smoke check was least helpful. Testing covered all endings, controller/mobile emulation, screenshots, offline audio, WebGL/WebGPU and multiplayer with latency and loss. WebKit rendered successfully; Firefox simulation passed, but rendered Firefox was unavailable here. Real iOS Safari and physical-controller testing were unavailable.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** The deterministic loop and World3D foundation were most useful. Pose, recoil and startup-readiness assumptions caused trouble. Persistent fire was the largest custom system; coordinate systems, shader warmup and networking were hardest. Changes added custom vehicle drawing and missing GPU-flag compatibility. A documented first-person scaffold would help most.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** The pillars and verified recipes gave clear direction. Campaign versus demo scope was the main ambiguity. Integrating survival, story, hands and networking was hardest. I would add executable acceptance fixtures and distinguish mandatory slice content from campaign expansion.\n\nThese details are also embedded in About/Credits."}}
